  "interpretation": [
    "Default core reads return private user/session/account information despite native revocation. The independent new same-actor session makes list-sessions token disclosure distinguishable from replay of the already cached original session.",
    "Default unlink changes authentication-account business state under the revoked session; this is not permitted session/security bookkeeping.",
    "The queried disableCookieCache=false unlink/change-password variants denied without mutation. No query-override bypass is confirmed.",
    "No raw secret values are published. Returned token fields do not establish session takeover.",
    "This is a confirmed bounded finding from completed cases, not a final suite, browser, provider or cleanup verdict."
  ],
  "boundedRepairScope": "Enforce current persisted session and account authority for admitted core sensitive reads/account mutations while preserving authorized credential/session operations and existing reviewed profile behavior; refresh actual-source closure and test all affected routes before closure.",
